general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "infamous", "type": "name"}, {"content": "famous for something which is considered bad", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The musician had some infamous parties.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about jobs and fame.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "notorious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "known for something bad", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He's notorious for missing concerts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bad press", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when negative things are published about someone or something in a newspaper or on television", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He received a lot of bad press after the scandal. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "media", "type": "name"}, {"content": "television, Internet, newspapers, magazines and radio combined as a group ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Has the media been tough on you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sensationalize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to embellish in order to make more exciting", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They sensationalized the story.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "press", "type": "name"}, {"content": " those who report or publish the news (newspapers, television, radio, etc.)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a blogger, I am also part of the press.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "publicist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone responsible for increasing the popularity of a person or company", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I really need to fire my publicist.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a list of questions to ask a famous celebrity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I conduct an interview with a celebrity. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I provide feedback using stress.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I respond to interview questions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Pretend you run your own blog and you are about to interview your favorite celebrity. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose a celebrity to interview. It can be anyone, living or dead.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a minimum of ten questions to ask.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Role-play the interview with your partner playing the part of the celebrity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If they answer any of the questions incorrectly, correct them by stressing the appropriate answer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Reverse the roles and try again.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tonic, Contrastive, Emphatic and New Information Stress", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are various types of stress used when speaking English.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tonic stress</span> refers to the syllable in a word which receives the most stress in an intonation unit. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Well, let's go with <span class=\"strong\">no</span>table. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to point out the difference between one object and another, you use <span class=\"strong\">contrastive stress</span>. It tends to be used with determiners such as 'this', 'that', 'these' and 'those'.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br><span class=\"italic\">Anyway, it was a <span class=\"strong\">two</span>-day bender, not <span class=\"strong\">three</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">To emphasize</span> a word, you can change the stress from the principal word to another content word. By choosing a word other than the one you normally stress, you put emphasis on the new one.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">You can call me Ms. Davis or Sally, but definitely <span class=\"strong\">not</span> baby.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sentence stress gives English its <SPAN CLASS=\"STRONG\"> rhythm </span> or \"beat\".", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you<span class=\"strong\"> stress new information</span>, you pronounce it with more breath force, since it is more prominent. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reduction of Have in Past Modals and in Auxiliary Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you use auxiliary verbs like<span class=\"italic\"> have</span>, it is common to reduce it in conversation. </br></br>  In English, not every word or syllable is pronounced fully.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you reduce the sound of <span class=\"italic\">have</span> it sounds like <span class=\"strong\">uv</span> or <span class=\"strong\">iv</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read each sentence in its full form:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">could have</span> just skipped it, like I did that concert.</br> It sounds like your bad attitude <span class=\"strong\">might have</span> been a factor in their reporting. </br>I <span class=\"strong\">must have</span> got my schedule mixed up. </br>I <span class=\"strong\">would have</span> been more careful.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now read them and reduce the pronunciation of the auxiliary verb <span class=\"italic\">have</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">could've</span> just skipped it, like I did that concert.  could_uv</br> It sounds like your bad attitude <span class=\"strong\">might've</span> been a factor in their reporting. might_uv</br> I <span class=\"strong\">must've</span> got my schedule mixed up. must_uv</br> I <span class=\"strong\">would've</span> been more careful. would_uv", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about fame and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can use different tones to stress, contrast or emphasize information.", "type": 